                        }
                        deps (raw-identifier-casts)
                        log (
                            {
                                at 2026-09-08T15:16:26.560524Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @note
                                text "Shape of the work, as spiked and then reverted out of fad22bef so that commit could land green on its own. TypeName gains a `verbatim: bool` plus a `TypeName::custom(text)` constructor, short-circuiting `to_sql_string` to `raw_text()`; `Expr::cast_as_custom` becomes `self.cast_as_type(TypeName::custom(type_expr))`; `Function::Cast` and the `drop_right_as_hack` in `prepare_binary_expr` become dead and are deleted; `source_read_cast` loses the second match arm fad22bef added. Two rule bodies go stale with it and must be swept in the same commit: `sql.render.cast-param-type` v1 currently specifies both shapes explicitly (\"on both cast shapes ... and a `Value` in the left operand of a `BinOper::As`\"), and `sql.ast.func` still lists `cast_as` among the `Func` helpers though `Func::cast_as` was already deleted in fad22bef — that one is stale on main right now. Verified green at 1353/1353 in the spike before revert; the goldens it moves are the ones fad22bef already re-pinned."
                            }

                            {
                                at 2026-09-08T17:03:33.750159Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @note
                                text "Probe: checking whether the note write itself is what fails lint."
                                after_done true
                            }

                            {
                                at 2026-10-18T14:09:12.018449Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @note
                                text "Re-checked 2026-10-18 against sql.ast.cast-shape at +1, the node having been marked done at +0 (v1 added as_range and the entity layer's created-range casts). The code meets the rule: one node, SimpleExpr::AsEnum(Box<TypeName>, Box<SimpleExpr>); Function has no Cast variant; as_enum, cast_as, cast_as_type (on Expr and on SimpleExpr), cast_as_raw, as_range, the entity layer's enum and created-range casts, ActiveEnum::as_enum, CreatedRange::into_expr and the derive's select_as/save_as all build it; verbatim text is a private field of TypeName; one render arm; source_read_cast and codegen match the one shape. The rule text was wrong in one place: it said verbatim type text is reachable only through cast_as_raw, but TypeName::raw is public and called directly (with cast_as_type, and in DDL through ColumnType::Named). Safety holds through the &'static str bound, so the rule (+2) now names TypeName::raw's callers as the finite list and lists SimpleExpr's spellings; every pinned site was re-read and re-pinned. Still open, filed separately: the structural test every_cast_spelling_builds_one_node_shape and entity_layer_casts_build_the_one_cast_node were not extended for v1, so as_range and the created-range casts are held only by CAST( render goldens."
                                after_done true
                            }

                            {
                                at 2026-10-18T14:25:43.288969Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @note
                                text "Delivered again at the current rule version (sql.ast.cast-shape +2), on the re-check recorded above; the earlier commit carried a non-delivery type, so it did not refresh the node's evidence."
                                after_done true
                            }

                            {
                                at 2026-10-18T15:34:23.564669Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @note
                                text "Delivered again at sql.ast.cast-shape +2: merging branches cut before the 2026-10-18 re-check (c745e19b, 1ecaad8f, f9db65b7) restored the node's stale rule_versions_seen through the plan merge driver (filed in nplan's DEFECTS.md)."
                                after_done true
                            }
                        )
