                title "Make fallible after-save and after-delete hooks atomic with persistence"
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-09-05T14:52:36.046096Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Audit CONFIRMED as described; inherited SeaORM semantics, spec wording overpromises. insert/update/delete run before-hook → exec → after-hook on a plain &C ConnectionTrait (active_model.rs:242-246, 277-280, 303-313); no path opens a transaction (begin needs &mut), so an Err from after_save/after_delete propagates AFTER the row was durably written/deleted. Spec entity.active-model.hooks says \"An Err from any hook aborts the operation\" — true only for before-hooks. Scenario: fallible after_save → insert returns Err yet row exists; retry duplicates. Callers can already pass a DatabaseTransaction for atomicity. Fix options: (a) honest-docs — amend spec+docs to state after-hook errors don't roll back, recommend caller-owned tx (S, non-breaking); (b) true atomicity — entry points demand transactional connection (L, breaking). Verdict leans (a) given scoped-transaction design. Bumps entity.active-model.hooks→+1 either way."
                    }

