                kind @blocker
                text "Found while fixing pipeline-renamed-column-order and left unfixed there as a distinct fault. When a projection draws the same bare column name from two different sources, for example select of cake.id, fruit.name and cake.name, deduplication drops the renamed column rather than keeping both. Same prqlc namespace-tree cause as its siblings: `this` is resolved by walking a tree keyed by name, so two columns competing for one name cannot both survive the walk and one is silently lost. As with distinct-drops-computed-column the behaviour is identical settled and unsettled, so the settle mechanism neither causes nor cures it. The join case matters more than it looks, because drawing a same-named column from both sides of a join is ordinary rather than exotic; id and name collide between almost any pair of tables."
            }

