    {
        id campaign-refuses-stale-build
        title "A campaign run refuses a native build older than its source"
        kind @fix
        sealed true
        log (
            {
                at 2026-09-15T16:37:58.593416Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @blocker
                text "live_campaign.py runs against whatever native extension happens to be sitting in target/generative-build, without checking that it was built from the source now checked out. On 2026-09-15 a full profile ran against a bridge built at revision 721003fb while HEAD was three commits further on, so a fix landed in f80e61f1 was neither confirmed nor refuted and the run silently reported the defect it was supposed to have cleared. build.json already records the exact identity needed to catch this — source_sha256, revision, interpreter, rustc and the maturin version — and prepare compares that identity to decide whether to rebuild. Nothing calls prepare from the run path, so the evidence exists and is simply never consulted. Two separable behaviours are worth having: a run should refuse outright when the recorded source digest does not match the tree it is about to test, because a campaign that silently tests the wrong code can report fixed or still-broken about something that is not what is checked out, and that is worse than not running at all. Rebuilding automatically is the friendlier option but hides the cost of a thirty-second link behind what the caller thinks is a read-only operation, so refusing with the command to run is probably the better default. Second failure from the same session worth fixing alongside: that run also collided with three agents exercising the same PostgreSQL, and 2947 of its 2972 findings were FixtureFailure with the cause requested worker has no active owned fixture. The runner provisions per-worker fixtures and has no way to notice that another process is using the server, so it reported a catastrophic-looking result that meant nothing. An advisory lock taken on the maintenance database for the duration of a run would make that collision an immediate refusal rather than three thousand phantom findings."
            }

            {
                at 2026-09-16T23:45:58.899831Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @status
                text "Todo → Doing (nplan start)"
            }

