            {
                id query-raw-template-words
                title "Verbatim SQL says raw, validated SQL says template, and custom says nothing"
                kind @refactor
                deps (query-dead-surface-gone)
                sealed true
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-09-19T23:11:56.726417Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @decision
                        text "The word \"custom\" currently spans the entire safety spectrum: cust_with_values/CustomExpr are validated arity-checked templates, Expr::cust and the extra methods are verbatim Into<String>, order_by_customs/partition_by_custom(s) are verbatim ToString, custom_keyword/ColumnDef::custom/IndexType::Custom are verbatim wearing IntoIden, and BinOper::Custom is verbatim but honestly &'static str — five bounds for one semantic and one word for five semantics. Decided vocabulary, ratified 2026-09-20: unmarked = quoted identifier; raw = verbatim, accepting only &'static str or a RawSql newtype; template = validated and Result-returning (cust_with_values -> Expr::template, CustomExpr -> SqlTemplate). This aligns pgorm-query with the vocabulary pgorm proper already uses consistently — query_raw, execute_raw, SelectorRaw, from_raw_sql, TypeName::raw_text all mean exactly \"trusted SQL text\". Exit check, greppable: the strings \"custom\" and \"cust\" appear nowhere in pgorm-query's public API. Most of the offenders are deleted by query-dead-surface-gone rather than renamed, which is why that node is a dep."
                    }

