    {
        id prqlc-distinct-on-dropped-key
        title "A DISTINCT ON key the projection drops still orders the deduplication"
        kind @fix
        sealed true
        log (
            {
                at 2026-09-24T00:02:07.653268Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @blocker
                text "Found by the fork agent while fixing prqlc-literal-ordinal in the fork (branch pgorm/deterministic-star-expansion). When a group key is a computed expression and the final projection drops it, prqlc's DISTINCT ON lowering still names the key by its alias in the derived ORDER BY: `from cake | derive {x = id + 1} | group {x} (sort id | take 1) | select {name, id}` compiles to a DISTINCT ON whose ORDER BY cites `x`, a column the SELECT list no longer carries, and PostgreSQL rejects it at execution with SQLSTATE 42703 (undefined column). Verified against live PostgreSQL 16. Reachable from pgorm only through the prql! macro, which compiles raw PRQL text through the fork; pgorm's pipeline builder never constructs the shape. Fixed in the fork at 4ff45819 (\"order DISTINCT ON by a key's expression when the projection drops it\"): the derived ORDER BY now writes the key's expression when the projection drops it. Lands in pgorm through the same re-pin that carries prqlc-group-by-wildcard (dd9a0fee) and prqlc-literal-ordinal (84f572a8)."
            }

