                kind @blocker
                text "The full profile declares `time_sec: 3`, and sqlmap has never been given it. `scanner_args` in security/sqlmap/adapter/src/harness/mod.rs hardcodes `--time-sec 1`. The retired harness.py did the same: its argument list, removed in bf12bd48, carried a literal `\"--time-sec\", \"1\"`. Commit 041e4412 (\"Let a timed sleep stand clear of the scan's own load\") is the change that raised time_sec from 1 to 3, but it touched only profiles.json, README.md and the plan, never the invocation. The recorded evidence agrees: every T-control `command.json` under target/sqlmap-ci/full-01, the run behind the 2026-09-17 acceptance, records `--time-sec 1`. The adapter test `command_options_and_encoding_match_python` pins the bug, because it builds the command from `profiles[\"full\"]` and asserts `--time-sec 1`. The profile declares four other settings the harness also never reads: `concurrency` (hardcoded `--threads 1`), `retries` (`--retries 0`), `http_timeout_seconds` (`--timeout 15`) and `postgres_statement_timeout_seconds` (hardcoded `statement_timeout=10000` / `'10s'` on the container, the fixture role and the direct-regression role). These match their hardcoded values only by coincidence, so editing any of them in profiles.json would silently change nothing. The harness reads only cases, techniques, level, risk and case_timeout_seconds. That leaves the profile, the thing security.sqlmap.profiles makes the version-controlled declaration of a run, describing settings the scan does not use, and it leaves two acceptance documents recording a time_sec the scanner never ran."
            }

