    {
        id embedded-index-kinds
        title "A table constraint embedded in CREATE TABLE is always one PostgreSQL accepts"
        kind @fix
        sealed true
        log (
            {
                at 2026-09-25T05:07:37.037603Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @blocker
                text "Flagged independently by three missions (95840ed2's embedding test, a1653e01's index forms, bf3bf75d's deferrability). `TableCreateStatement::index(..)` embeds an `IndexCreateStatement` as a table constraint, and the index type admits shapes a table constraint cannot take: a `Plain` (non-unique, non-primary) kind renders `CONSTRAINT \"idx\" (\"col\")`, which PostgreSQL rejects, and a partial-index predicate or an expression column has no table-constraint spelling either. `sql.ddl.create-table` documents both as known gaps. bf3bf75d introduced `IndexConstraint`, the wrapper `index()`/`primary_key()` now take, which is the natural place to rule them out: only a unique or primary-key index with plain column entries (and optional INCLUDE and deferrability) should convert into an `IndexConstraint`; a plain kind, a predicate or an expression entry should not be representable on the embedded path, and should remain available on standalone `CREATE INDEX`. Establish the accepted table-constraint shapes live, make the refused ones unrepresentable (compile_fail doctests), sweep callers (codegen emits embedded indexes), and update sql.ddl.create-table / sql.ddl.index-create."
            }

            {
                at 2026-09-30T17:02:45.600184Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @status
                text "Todo → Doing (nplan start)"
            }

            {
                at 2026-09-30T17:03:08.935552Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @decision
                text "Filed prescription refined (agent opus-scope-mission-2): rather than letting \"only a unique or primary-key index with plain column entries\" convert into IndexConstraint — a conversion whose validity is runtime state of an IndexCreateStatement, so it could only be fallible, not typed — IndexConstraint becomes a builder of its own (unique / unique_nulls_not_distinct / primary_key constructors taking the first key column as a Name; col, name, include, deferrability). IndexCreateStatement no longer converts into one and is standalone-only: IndexKind loses PrimaryKey, primary()/is_primary_key()/StandaloneIndexKind/IndexKind::standalone/IndexCreateStatement::deferrability are deleted, and TableCreateStatement::primary_key() goes (index() is the one embedder; the key kind is the constraint's own). NULLS NOT DISTINCT is a constructor, not a setter, because PRIMARY KEY NULLS NOT DISTINCT is a syntax error. Re-verified live on PG 16.15: in a table constraint DESC, ASC, an opclass, COLLATE, an expression, WHERE, USING <method>, a bare (kind-less) key list and PRIMARY KEY NULLS NOT DISTINCT are all syntax errors; UNIQUE NULLS NOT DISTINCT, INCLUDE and DEFERRABLE are accepted; hash/gin/gist/brin all refuse unique indexes. Codegen consequence: a CREATE UNIQUE INDEX is folded into the table as the unique constraint it enforces, so a DESC key column or a non-btree access method on one is now a named rejection (it cannot be carried and must not be dropped); explicit ASC (the default) is accepted; IF NOT EXISTS is a property of the folded-away statement and is dropped, documented."
            }

            {
                at 2026-10-01T21:30:43.702126Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @status
                text "Doing → Done (nplan complete)"
            }
        )
    }

    {
        id cursor-bind-jiff-gate
        title "pgorm builds without with-jiff: the cursor's civil-datetime binding names jiff ungated"
        kind @fix
        sealed true
        log (
            {
                at 2026-10-01T21:31:54.195734Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @blocker
                text "Found while landing embedded-index-kinds (2026-09-30): `cargo nextest run -p pgorm-codegen` and `cargo check -p pgorm-codegen --all-targets` fail to compile pgorm with E0433 \"cannot find module or crate `jiff`\" in src/executor/cursor_bind.rs, at the PG_EPOCH const, civil_micros_since_pg_epoch and bind_civil_datetime. pgorm-codegen's dev-dependency is `pgorm = { path = \"../\", default-features = false, features = [\"macros\"] }`, and jiff is an optional dependency of pgorm (`with-jiff = [\"jiff\"]`), but cursor_bind.rs names `jiff::` with no `#[cfg(feature = \"with-jiff\")]`; the ungated paths arrived with dd8ecb09 (hand-encoding the civil datetime). A workspace-wide build hides it by feature unification, which is why `cargo nextest run --workspace` and `nplan check` stay green. minimal-feature-build (Done) fixed the same contract for rust_decimal, so this is a regression of it. Acceptance: pgorm compiles under `--no-default-features` and `--no-default-features --features macros` again (gate the civil-datetime bind path on with-jiff, or reach jiff's types through a dependency that is always present), and a check that builds pgorm without feature unification, in the configurations minimal-feature-build named, guards it so it cannot regress silently a second time."
            }

            {
                at 2026-10-01T21:43:20.560679Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @status
                text "Todo → Doing (nplan start)"
            }

            {
                at 2026-10-01T22:11:02.956694Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @decision
                text "Two corrections to the filed text. (1) minimal-feature-build left no guard to extend: d4653f88 made rust_decimal required and recorded the contract in exec.decode.types, but added no check, CI job or test that builds pgorm without feature unification — its acceptance was a one-off manual check. The guard is therefore new, built on the existing mechanism (an nplan platform in .config/nplan/config.styx, `rust-features`), with the manifests in its file scope so a feature-edge change re-runs it: `cargo check -p pgorm --lib` with --no-default-features, with --no-default-features --features macros, and with the defaults. The Decimal-enabled configuration it named no longer exists. (2) Gating the bind path on with-jiff would be wrong, not just one of two options: Value::DateTime is an unconditional variant of pgorm-query's value model, so the bind path must encode it in every configuration, and a gated path would change a naive datetime's wire encoding by feature. jiff is compiled in every configuration anyway (pgorm-query and tokio-postgres's with-jiff-0_2 depend on it), so it is now a required dependency of pgorm, as rust_decimal is, and with-jiff gates the conversion surface only. exec.decode.types+3 records this and replaces its stale chrono text. Sensitivity: restoring HEAD's Cargo.toml (jiff optional) made the new minimal and macros-only checks fail with the four E0433s; default passed, as it must."
            }

            {
                at 2026-10-01T22:11:03.011048Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @status
                text "Doing → Done (nplan complete)"
            }
        )
    }

