            {
                id pg18-virtual-generated
                title "A generated column can be VIRTUAL as well as STORED"
                kind @feat
                deps (pg18-test-server pg-query-18)
                sealed true
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-10-06T12:50:41.451209Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "The sql.ddl rules (docs/spec/sql-ddl.md) currently refuse VIRTUAL generated columns because \"the builder cannot know which release it is writing for\", and name the shape a future addition takes. With 18 as the target, the builder can write it. Add VIRTUAL beside STORED on ColumnSpec::Generated (or its successor). Check live what 18 refuses for a virtual column (indexes on it, a user-defined type, a volatile expression and so on). Cover the entity derive (#[pgorm(generated...)] or equivalent), schema-gen, codegen's DDL path (parse_schema needs pg-query-18) and Python if it exposes generated columns. Note PostgreSQL 18's default: a bare GENERATED ALWAYS AS (...) is now VIRTUAL, where 17 required STORED. pgorm must always render the kind explicitly so it never depends on the server default."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-10-06T15:36:13.737569Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "pg-query-18 landed the 18 grammar. Two places now wait on this node: pgorm-query/tests/postgres/table.rs generated_column_is_always_stored, whose tripwire asserted the oracle refuses VIRTUAL, now asserts the oracle accepts it (the refusal is only the missing constructor, per sql.ddl.column-def+9's text, which this node revises); and codegen's DDL bridge refuses a VIRTUAL column by name (\"a VIRTUAL generated column\", codegen.ddl.unsupported+6), including a bare GENERATED ALWAYS AS (...), which 18 reads as VIRTUAL (Constraint.generated_kind \"v\"). Replace that refusal with the reading when the entity model can hold it."
                    }

                    {
