            {
                id pg18-temporal-keys
                title "A table key can end WITHOUT OVERLAPS and a foreign key can reference a PERIOD"
                kind @feat
                deps (pg18-test-server pg-query-18)
                sealed true
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-10-06T12:50:41.503406Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "PostgreSQL 18 adds temporal keys. PRIMARY KEY / UNIQUE (a, b, valid_at WITHOUT OVERLAPS), where the last column is a range or multirange and the key is enforced by a GiST index, which needs btree_gist for scalar columns. FOREIGN KEY (a, PERIOD valid_at) REFERENCES t (a, PERIOD valid_at). These interact with TableKey<K> (pgorm-query/src/table/key.rs, d982a21d), a non-empty ordered column list. Only the last column may be WITHOUT OVERLAPS, so put that in the type, not in a per-column flag that could land in the middle. Ranges exist end to end since 6006221d. The extension requirement (CREATE EXTENSION btree_gist) is already buildable (sql.ddl.extension). Needs pg-query-18 for the oracle and codegen. Check each refusal live and record SQLSTATEs."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-10-06T15:36:13.810589Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "pg-query-18 landed the 18 grammar. Codegen's DDL bridge refuses both shapes by name until this node builds them (codegen.ddl.unsupported+6, pgorm-codegen/src/sql_schema/table.rs reject_constraint_features): Constraint.without_overlaps -> \"a WITHOUT OVERLAPS key\", fk_with_period/pk_with_period -> \"a PERIOD foreign key\". It also refuses a NOT ENFORCED foreign key (is_enforced false at table level, CONSTR_ATTR_NOT_ENFORCED at column level), which 18 added too and no node owns yet."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-10-07T01:12:05.317894Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
