            {
                id entity-relation-not-enforced
                title "An entity relation can say its foreign key is NOT ENFORCED, so codegen can read one"
                kind @feat
                deps (pg18-not-enforced)
                sealed true
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-10-07T01:09:33.583206Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Found by pg18-not-enforced (cdcc02d6). PostgreSQL 18 lets a foreign key be NOT ENFORCED: recorded, never checked, with no referential triggers, so its ON DELETE / ON UPDATE actions never fire. pgorm-query now writes one (TableForeignKey::enforcement, ConstraintChange::Enforced / NotEnforced, sql.ddl.enforcement), but codegen still refuses it (\"a NOT ENFORCED constraint\", codegen.ddl.unsupported+9) because the entity model cannot hold it: RelationDef has on_delete, on_update and fk_name and no enforcement, DeriveRelation has no attribute for it, and Schema::create_table_from_entity turns every owned relation into an enforced foreign key, so a schema regenerated from a generated entity would enforce what the source did not, and load_one, which errors on an unmatched key, would meet the orphans a NOT ENFORCED key admits. Deferrability is in the same position (codegen refuses a deferrable constraint and RelationDef has none). Decide whether an entity relation carries its key's constraint attributes (enforcement, and deferrability with it) and what load_one / load_many and the graph should do over a relation whose key is not enforced; then a RelationDef field and DeriveRelation attribute, the From<RelationDef> for ForeignKeyCreateStatement mapping, codegen's reader and writer, the generative campaign's emitters, and Python's registered entities."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-10-07T02:56:59.169301Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Found while landing pg18-temporal-keys (d33e0801): the DDL bridge refuses a NOT ENFORCED foreign key, but EntityTransformer::transform, which takes caller-built TableCreateStatements, reads one as a plain relation without a word (TableForeignKey::get_enforcement is never consulted). pg18-temporal-keys made the gate refuse a WITHOUT OVERLAPS key and a PERIOD foreign key in a caller-built statement (refuse_temporal_constraints, codegen.entity.transform+10), for the same reason the bridge refuses them; a NOT ENFORCED foreign key belongs beside them until this node lets the entity hold it."
                    }

