                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @status
                        text "Doing → Done (nplan complete)"
                    }
                )
            }
        )
        log (
            {
                at 2026-10-06T12:50:41.172836Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @decision
                text "Operator 2026-10-06: \"move the test server to the latest version of postgres and ensure we support it all.\" The latest released version is 18 (18.6). 19 is at beta 4, with RC1 on 2026-10-15 and GA planned for 2026-10-29, and beta 4 reverted several features, so the target is 18 now and pg19-test-server follows GA. The operator chose this over keeping 16 and adding a second 17+ server, which means nothing proves 16 or 17 compatibility afterwards and 18 becomes the de facto floor. A survey on 2026-10-06 (Sonnet, read-only, its own PostgreSQL 18.6 container) found:\n\n(A) The whole workspace passes on 18.6 unchanged, 1676/1676, so the move is pins and docs rather than fixes. Doctests, pgorm-python, sqlmap and the campaign were not run on 18.\n\n(B) Pin sites: .github/workflows/python.yml (postgresql-16 / postgresql@16 and PGORM_TEST_PG_BIN in both jobs), security/sqlmap/pins.json:10 (postgres:16.13-bookworm digest) and the acceptance records citing 16.13, security/generative/src/pgorm_campaign/fixtures.py:13 (the same image) with its asserting tests (test_campaign_report.py:25,92), pgorm-python/DISTRIBUTION.md:30 and ACCEPTANCE.md:29,66, and the local pgorm-test container (postgres:16, port 54329).\n\n(C) pg_query 6.2.0 embeds libpg_query 17-6.x, the PostgreSQL 17 grammar. Verified live: 18-only syntax fails to parse — VIRTUAL generated columns, named NOT NULL with NOT VALID / NO INHERIT, WITHOUT OVERLAPS keys, FOREIGN KEY ... PERIOD — which would refuse it in sql!, codegen's parse_schema and the identifier oracle. libpg_query 18.0.0 (May) and 18.1.0 (2026-09-30, Postgres 18.6 plus a fix for an out-of-bounds bug in pg_query_normalize, GHSA-6ggm-xmc9-8ffg) are released. pg_query.rs's upgrade, PR pganalyze/pg_query.rs#79 \"Release 18.0.0\", is open and unmerged; it was re-requested for review on 2026-10-01. pgorm calls parse, scan and fingerprint, not normalize.\n\n(D) Features: MERGE's 17 additions, already filed as merge-beyond-pg16 and moved here. RETURNING OLD/NEW already works through quoted \"old\".\"col\" (verified live); the WITH (OLD AS o, NEW AS n) rename does not. VIRTUAL generated columns; WITHOUT OVERLAPS and PERIOD; named, NOT VALID and NO INHERIT NOT NULL; uuidv7()/uuidv4(), reachable today through Func::named; ALTER COLUMN SET/DROP EXPRESSION; SQL/JSON's JSON_TABLE and JSON_QUERY/VALUE/EXISTS, whose COLUMNS / PATH / ON ERROR grammar Func::named cannot express. COPY's 17/18 changes are out of scope per sql.scope (COPY belongs to the driver surface). The restricted-keyword list is unchanged in 18.\n\n\"Support it all\" is read as building every in-scope item. The SQL/JSON node is therefore built, not left as a scope question, unless the operator says otherwise."
            }
        )
    }

    {
        id python-typing-check-symlinked-tmp
        title "The typing checker's installed-package check passes when the temporary directory sits behind a symlink"
        kind @fix
        log (
            {
                at 2026-10-06T14:15:01.552943Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @note
                text "Found by pg18-test-server (84d97a35) while re-recording pgorm-python's acceptance on PostgreSQL 18, and unrelated to the server version. pgorm-python/checks/typing.py installed_metadata() resolves the package root (`root = Path(pgorm.__file__).resolve().parent`) and then asserts `Path(_native.__file__).parent == root` without resolving the native module's path. distribution.py installs each wheel into a venv under tempfile's directory. On macOS that is $TMPDIR=/var/folders/..., reached through the /var -> /private/var symlink, so the two paths differ by the prefix and the assertion fails before any typing runs. Reproduced in a fresh venv from the same wheel: the native module's parent is /var/folders/.../site-packages/pgorm while root is /private/var/folders/.../site-packages/pgorm. The failure surfaced as the distribution phase of checks/acceptance.py failing on 2026-10-06. The stderr is not captured into distribution.log, so the log shows only CalledProcessError. CI's macOS job passes because its runner's temporary directory is not behind a symlink, and the 2026-10-06 acceptance record ran with TMPDIR set to its resolved path (pgorm-python/ACCEPTANCE.md says so). Fix: resolve the native module's path before comparing (`Path(_native.__file__).resolve().parent == root`). Consider also surfacing the child's stderr when the metadata program fails. Acceptance: checks/acceptance.py passes through tests/with_postgres.py under macOS's default TMPDIR, and ACCEPTANCE.md's TMPDIR paragraph is removed."
            }

            {
