    {
        id created-multiranges
        title "A multirange a schema creates binds and decodes, though the driver reports it as a simple type"
        kind @feat
        deps (created-range-types)
        log (
            {
                at 2026-10-07T10:38:10.018504Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @note
                text "Split from range-consumers-beyond-builtins (2026-10-07). A multirange a schema creates is refused both ways (cursor_bind_range::bind_multirange, MultirangeSql::accepts). The cause: tokio-postgres 0.7.18's TYPEINFO_QUERY (src/prepare.rs) joins pg_range only ON r.rngtypid = t.oid, so a created multirange (typtype 'm', whose pg_range row is keyed by rngmultitypid) arrives as Kind::Simple with no subtype. Routes found, none taken: (1) Driver: a lookup that also joins on rngmultitypid would report Kind::Multirange(subtype). That is a tokio-postgres change, either an upstream PR or a fork pgorm does not carry today. (2) SQL: bind through the multirange's own variadic constructor over an array of its ranges, which the driver types correctly. Checked live on 18.6 with a prepared parameter: floatmultirange(VARIADIC $1) with $1 typed floatrange[] builds {[1,2),[3,4)}, and builds {} from '{}'. Decode through ARRAY(SELECT unnest(col)), which is floatrange[]. Both are rewrites the entity layer would have to own, as save_as/select_as own an enum's cast. (3) A subtype supplied by the caller cannot be checked against the server's type, and could send bytes the server reads as another type. Depends on created-range-types for naming the multirange."
            }

            {
                at 2026-10-07T15:22:46.459607Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @decision
                text "Operator 2026-10-07 chose route (b) for created range types (see created-range-types' decision note): Value stays at 16 bytes, and a created-range value travels as a text literal cast to its named type. A created multirange follows the same principle. Bind through the variadic constructor that range-consumers-beyond-builtins verified live (floatmultirange(VARIADIC $1) with $1 typed floatrange[]), or as a text literal cast to the named multirange type, whichever proves simpler and safe. Decode through the route it recorded (ARRAY(SELECT unnest(col))), since tokio-postgres reports a created multirange as a simple type. The multirange type's name is caller-named and registered in the identifier oracle."
            }

            {
                at 2026-10-07T18:23:33.00887Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @status
                text "Todo → Doing (nplan start)"
