                at 2026-10-18T16:10:07.520311Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @decision
                text "describe() now reports each relation's condition_type (\"all\"/\"any\") and on_condition (present/absent bool), rather than the rule stopping implying it: both decide what a join by the relation reads, condition_type is a two-value enum and on_condition a Rust closure over the join's aliases with no rendering of its own, so a bool is the honest report. python.entities +3 says enforcement and deferrability change what the server holds the key's rows to, not the join. The WINDOW clause's one named window is a pgorm-query capability gap, not wording: PostgreSQL's WINDOW clause takes a list, SelectStatement::window holds Option<(Name, WindowStatement)>, and a second call silently drops the first name, so an item over it fails at the server (42704) instead of at construction; python.statements +4 states the behaviour, Rust is unchanged here. Truth testing: JsonInput and WindowFunction now refuse; the schema module's CreateTable, CreateIndex and DDL (and Compiled) still evaluate truthy and were left alone because sql-views is editing src/schema in parallel."
