                at 2026-10-18T19:03:45.587933Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @decision
                text "Python's Select gains union, union_all, intersect, intersect_all, except_ and except_all, each Rust's SelectStatement::union with one of the six UnionTypes and the arm read through PySelect::embedded (its tie limit checked as it is read; a non-Select arm is a TypeError). Naming follows pgorm-napi's union/unionAll/intersect/intersectAll/except/exceptAll in snake case; except is a Python keyword, so except_, as from_/where_/with_. Semantics are Rust's, unchanged: the receiver's ORDER BY/LIMIT/OFFSET/tie limit render after the last arm whenever set, its WITH precedes every arm, arms render flat in call order so PostgreSQL's precedence regroups an INTERSECT after a UNION/EXCEPT (documented and tested live, not changed: parity with Rust and JavaScript). A recursive view's step arm must read the view by its bare name (the WITH RECURSIVE name); a qualified name is 42P01. python.statements +6, python.schema-views +1 (caveat replaced by the recursive-view requirement)."
                after_done true
            }
        )
    }

