                text "Found by sql-domains (2fa97891). PostgreSQL has no operator at all on a domain over an enum, not even d = d (42883), so every predicate and keyset cursor comparison on such a column fails at the server unless the column is cast to the enum; this is recorded in entity.traits.column.enum-cast but not handled. Make the ORM's value predicates (eq and friends, membership, between) and cursor bounds cast a domain-over-enum column to its enum, as save_as casts work for enums today, with live tests."
