                kind @note
                text "Found by domain-enum-remaining (596d21c2). The Rust pipeline casts a typed column's comparisons (typed_cast in src/pipeline/sources.rs), but `col(table, column)` and alias tokens carry no column type, and neither do the Python and JavaScript pipelines, so comparing such a column with a bound string fails with 42883. A fix needs the column's type at those points (from the bindings' entity registrations, or named by the caller) and an enum-capable cast, since CastType is a closed set. Settle where the type comes from before building."
            }

