                at 2026-10-23T19:22:04.71849Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @decision
                text "Operator 2026-10-23: \"yes\" to taking the column's type from its entity wherever one is known (the bindings' entity registrations, a typed source), and letting the caller name the type where none is. Also in scope (found by in-subquery-enum-shapes): the Python and JavaScript statement builders' subquery membership carries no column type either, so it gets none of the domain-over-enum casts."
            }

            {
                at 2026-10-25T23:33:44.800678Z
