            }

            {
                at 2026-10-25T23:34:10.811673Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @note
                text "Design: the type comes from the entity where one is known and is named by the caller where none is. Rust: Named::col(column) writes a named entity's column typed by the entity; ExprOps::compares_as(enum TypeName) names the enum for col() and alias tokens. Python/JS: pl.col(table, entity.col(name)) lowers through the registration's own Named::col; compares_as / comparesAs names the enum. JS EntityColumn.isIn/isNotIn (values and Select) go through ColumnTrait is_in/in_subquery. Python's statement builders have no subquery membership at all, so there was nothing to cast there; a statement builder's own expression stays SQL as written (the caller casts)."
                after_done true
            }
        )
    }

