            }

            {
                at 2026-10-30T13:24:14.310242Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @decision
                text "Operator 2026-10-30: \"everything you said, sure\", accepting all fourteen recommendations on the undecided differences. (1) literal: both bindings bind every plain operand, statements and pipelines alike, and both offer an explicit literal() in statements and pipelines. (2) row-count: a wrong row count is a DecodeError in both. (3) inference: Python infers a list as an array of one kind and a dict as JSON as JavaScript does, keeping the refusals of empty, all-null and mixed lists; a tuple stays refused. (4) raw-sql and (5) records: language differences, kept per binding. (6) names: one name each, mostly JavaScript's: where (never where_ or filter), query / one / optional (never fetch_* or one_opt), do_nothing, set, using, truncate_table, Aliased, Windowed, RowStream, PgormError, EntityGraph / EntityGraphQuery / EntityGraphCursor (freeing Graph for the model graph), PipelineExpr; Python's json_objectagg, json_arrayagg and DDL kept, so JavaScript spells jsonObjectagg, jsonArrayagg and DDL. (7) shapes: decided one at a time with a concrete proposal to the operator when each area is next worked on. (8) columns: Python's model and registered columns offer every expression method. (9) capabilities: capabilities(), require_capability(), UnsupportedCapabilityError and Value.snapshot() stay Python-only as the campaign's surface; Python gains entities(), graphs() and source_tuples(). (10) schema-api: Python adopts JavaScript's DDL builders and pending-ALTER typestates, its per-action functions deleted. (11) update-many-guard: a registered update_many() needs where or all_rows() in both. (12) argument errors: TypeError for an argument of the wrong type in both, ConstructionError only for a value that cannot become what pgorm sends. (13) a listener closed under a waiting pull ends the iteration in both. (14) TLS: both take PEM data as ca, Python keeping cafile as a convenience."
                after_done true
            }

