        title "Python reports an application hook's refusal as a ConstructionError, as bindings.entity-writes and JavaScript do"
        kind @fix
        sealed true
        log (
            {
                at 2026-10-31T17:06:51.520168Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @note
                text "Found by python-binding-decisions (merged 70cbc894). pgorm's Error::Custom, which an ActiveModelBehavior hook's refusal arrives as, still maps to DatabaseError in pgorm-python/src/errors.rs, while bindings.entity-writes says a hook's refusal is a ConstructionError and JavaScript's entity_failure maps it so. Python's transaction task uses the same Custom variant internally, so mapping every Custom to ConstructionError would misreport those; give the internal uses a variant or a typed error of their own first, then map the hook's refusal, with a live test of each."
            }

            {
                at 2026-10-31T22:54:44.640722Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @status
                text "Todo → Doing (nplan start)"
            }

