                kind @status
                text "Doing → Done (nplan complete)"
            }
        )
    }

    {
        id python-model-created-multirange
        title "Python's declared models decode a created multirange column, as bindings.models lists it"
        kind @feat
        sealed true
        log (
            {
                at 2026-10-31T17:06:51.690259Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @note
                text "Found by python-model-gaps (merged 0d1442b5). bindings.models lists a CreatedMultirange as a column kind, but a Python model column of one is refused with UnsupportedCapabilityError: Python's record decoder refuses created multiranges, which the existing created-range tests require. JavaScript's models decode them. Teach the record decoder a created multirange (its type and the range's subtype, as a created range is), lift the refusal, and add live tests of a model reading and writing one."
            }

            {
                at 2026-10-31T22:54:45.807746Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @status
                text "Todo → Doing (nplan start)"
            }

            {
                at 2026-11-01T01:22:41.527168Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @note
                text "Checked against the code (2026-11-01): JavaScript's models do not decode a created multirange either. A model declaring CreatedMultirange(\"floatmultirange\", \"f64\") writes one, but insert(..).returning().one() and find().all() both throw DecodeError \"column \\\"spans\\\" of type `app.floatmultirange` cannot be decoded: the type is not supported\", because the driver reports the column as a simple type and nothing casts it. Python's fix projects such a column cast to text, as pgorm's ColumnTrait::select_as does for an entity, and reads the text into the declared kind; JavaScript needs the same and has no node for it."
            }

            {
                at 2026-11-01T03:02:51.396983Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @status
                text "Doing → Done (nplan complete)"
            }
        )
    }

