    {
        id python-model-shapes
        title "Python's model writes are ModelInsert, ModelUpdate and ModelDelete, and a column's conversion and description are no public methods of its own, as JavaScript's are"
        kind @refactor
        sealed true
        log (
            {
                at 2026-10-31T20:00:20.040537Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @note
                text "Decisions (A) and (B) of the operator's 2026-10-31 answer (binding-spec-consolidation). (A) Split pgorm-python's ModelWrite (pgorm-python/python/pgorm/models/writes.py, queries.py) into ModelInsert, ModelUpdate and ModelDelete, each with only its own methods — an insert's on_conflict and upsert terminals, an update's where / all_rows and change terminals, a delete's where / all_rows — so mypy refuses a method of another kind, as TypeScript refuses it in pgorm-napi; delete ModelWrite. (B) Make Column.validate and Column.value private (they are write and decode machinery; Value(data, kind) is the public conversion), and delete Column.describe and EntityColumn.describe in favour of Model.describe() and Entity.describe(). Settle both under the shapes question in docs/spec/bindings-surface.json, update the generative campaign's emitters and dispatchers where they call any of these, and state the shapes in the shared rules."
            }

            {
                at 2026-10-31T20:26:37.708986Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @note
                text "Built (A) and (B). pgorm-python/python/pgorm/models/writes.py holds ModelInsert (statement Insert | None, an insert of no rows having none), ModelUpdate and ModelDelete over two private bases: _Write (model, statement, returning, execute, the refusing __bool__) and _Guarded (where, all_rows, inspect) for update and delete, so mypy types each write's statement exactly and reports another kind's method as attr-defined; an insert's inspect(terminal=) takes the upsert terminals and an update's the change terminals, any other a TypeError (a closed choice), where a wrong-kind terminal was UnsupportedCapabilityError. Column.validate/value became _validate/_value; Column.describe and the native EntityColumn.describe are gone, Model.describe() reporting the same per-column keys as before and Entity.describe()[\"columns\"] what EntityColumn.describe gave. Rules: bindings.models+3 (a Column has no method, Value(data, kind) the public conversion, what Model.describe() reports), bindings.model-writes+1 (the three kinds, each only its own methods), bindings.column-operators+1 (neither column describes itself); both bindings' annotations re-pinned, JavaScript's code unchanged. bindings-surface.json lists ModelInsert/ModelUpdate/ModelDelete as shared and drops the five undecided Python names and three JavaScript ones, the shapes question no longer naming model writes or column helpers. test_truth_testing.py lists the two bases in BASES (never built; each sampled through a write). Campaign: effects.py and the emitted reproducer's _execute test the three classes; dispatch_models.py and emit_python.py refuse an insert carrying a predicate as a ConstructionError, as they refuse a delete carrying assignments, since an insert no longer has where (the grammar never builds one)."
            }

            {
                at 2026-10-31T22:52:13.637711Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @status
                text "Doing → Done (nplan complete)"
            }
        )
    }

