                        at 2026-11-02T12:46:24.716433Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Answer (read-only survey of the macros, fixtures, tests and codegen, 2026-11-02): yes, four things, none needing the hand-assembled format once attributes say them. (1) Table and schema names computed at run time: an Entity struct with fields (tests/common/features/dyn_table_name_lazy_static.rs, tests/identifier_oracle/fixtures.rs:12-47); compact always emits a unit Entity with literal names, but a hybrid already works (compact Model with no table_name plus a hand-written Entity under DeriveEntity, pgorm-macros/tests/derive_entity_model_test.rs:313-337), so the entity-trait derive stays for that case. (2) Arbitrary select_as/save_as: compact only casts verbatim text (cast_as_raw); hand-written ones quote an alias or name the cast at run time (src/entity/column.rs:1126-1131, 1258-1263; fixtures.rs:142-144). (3) A column type as any expression (fixtures.rs:211-235): compact forces a ColumnType:: prefix. (4) An on_condition using its (left, right) arguments: compact wraps it in |_, _|. Everything else has an attribute: every ColumnDef builder, EntityName's table, schema and comment, PrimaryKeyTrait; RelationTrait is hand-written beside compact entities already. Nothing outside the repo's own fixtures and goldens uses the expanded format. Verdict per the operator's rule (the format stays only if it expresses something compact cannot): delete it, adding select_with/save_with, an expression column_type and a closure on_condition — macros.derive.one-form, delivered by derives.compact-only. Codegen's two formats also differ in behaviour: compact drops varchar(n)/char(n) lengths (filed as codegen-compact-string-length), and expanded keys json_key by the SQL name instead of the field's, so from_json misses renamed fields (dies with the format)."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-11-02T12:46:54.155916Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @status
