                        at 2026-11-05T00:23:36.656053Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @decision
                        text "Lead, 2026-11-05, pending operator override: build OneOfShape as proposed, with one implementation that Schema::create_one_of, OneOf::key/set/load and both bindings delegate to. (1) Add `const NAME: &'static str` (the variant's name) to OneOfTarget in the OneOf derive. The variant is the enum's identity and its author picks it, while a target's table name is a different thing that can collide across schemas. (2) There is one load path, the shape's per-target `WHERE key IN (..)`; the typed OneOf::load decodes its rows into each target's Model. reads_column also refuses a Related relation that carries an on_condition, as Error::Type before anything is sent, alongside its refusal of a via, a period or another column. The reference is held by foreign keys, so its target row always exists; an on_condition can only make a held key look absent, so it is refused rather than evaluated. Bump disjoint.one-of for it. (3) Scope: both declared models and registered enums, as the rule says. (4) Tagged key: Python (value, key), JavaScript [value, key], unless the bindings already spell a tagged value some other way (the disjoint kind accessors), in which case follow that precedent."
                    }
