    {
        id entity-composite-unique
        title "An entity declares a composite UNIQUE constraint, and codegen keeps one it reads"
        kind @feat
        sealed true
        log (
            {
                at 2026-11-03T03:53:21.038292Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @note
                text "Found by disjoint.codegen (bdfd9dcb): an entity cannot express a composite UNIQUE constraint (only a column's own unique and indexes). Codegen therefore drops one it reads: in a near-miss disjoint shape the base's UNIQUE (id, kind) is lost, and the kind table's relation onto that pair then makes create_table_from_entity write a foreign key PostgreSQL refuses (42830, no unique constraint matching the referenced columns). Give the Entity derive a container key for a named composite unique (bare column paths, e.g. unique(name = \"uq-x\", Column::A, Column::B)), render it in create_table_from_entity, have codegen emit it, and test the near-miss round trip live. Also from that node, both small: validate_identities checks a schema-qualified enum's name collisions as UpperCamel(\"schema.name\") (MarketListingCategory) rather than the Rust name actually written; and the disjoint name-clash check refuses a base table named like a derive macro (debug), more than it needs to."
            }

            {
                at 2026-11-03T10:26:47.812754Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @status
                text "Todo → Doing (nplan start)"
            }

            {
                at 2026-11-03T10:51:01.215259Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @status
                text "Doing → Done (nplan complete)"
            }
        )
    }

    {
        id codegen-enum-variant-names
        title "Generated disjoint enums compile clippy-clean whatever their tables are named"
        kind @fix
        sealed true
        log (
            {
                at 2026-11-03T08:39:56.190722Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @note
                text "Found by disjoint.codegen-unkinded (30391b0c): a generated disjoint enum can trip clippy::enum_variant_names when the generated module is private — kind table web_shop under base shop becomes Shop::WebShop, a variant ending in the enum's name — so a downstream crate running clippy -D warnings fails on code it did not write. The kinded generator has the same exposure. Decide between emitting #[allow(clippy::enum_variant_names)] on the generated enum (generated code the user does not hand-edit, as other generators do) and renaming, and test with a fixture whose table names trigger it, under clippy -D warnings."
            }

            {
                at 2026-11-03T10:10:11.920887Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @status
                text "Todo → Doing (nplan start)"
            }

            {
                at 2026-11-03T10:21:00.178339Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @decision
                text "Allow rather than rename: the variants are named by the schema (kind values, table names), the derive's default value is the variant's snake_case name, and clippy's enum_variant_names has three checks (a variant starting or ending with the enum's name, a prefix or postfix every variant shares) gated on a configurable threshold, so no renaming predicts it. codegen writes #[allow(clippy::enum_variant_names)] on every disjoint enum it generates, kinded and unkinded; the Disjoint derive puts it on <Enum>Kind, <Enum>ActiveModel and an unkinded kind enum (an allow on the program's enum does not reach them), and the ActiveEnum derive on {Enum}Variant, whose escaped variants (web_shop -> Web0x5Fshop) share a postfix whenever the values share a last word. Found, not fixed: codegen's Relation enum (three kind tables ending _shop give Relation { MallShop, PopUpShop, WebShop }) and the ActiveEnum enums codegen writes into pgorm_active_enums.rs (values web_shop, pop_up_shop, closed_shop) trip the same lint in a module not exported; fixing them changes every generated file's golden, the bindings' codegen fixtures included."
            }

            {
                at 2026-11-03T10:21:00.459265Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @status
                text "Doing → Done (nplan complete)"
            }
        )
    }

    {
        id unique-keys
        title "Unique keys round-trip: declared by entities and the bindings, written by schema generation, read back whole by codegen"
        kind @fix
        children (
            {
                id unique-key-virtual-refused
                title "The Entity derive refuses a VIRTUAL generated column inside unique(..), as the field-level unique does"
                kind @fix
                deps (entity-composite-unique)
