                        at 2026-11-03T14:52:21.693016Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Found by disjoint.codegen's near-miss tests (pre-existing): a table keyed by `id` with a foreign key `(id, kind)` onto another table's UNIQUE pair (the disjoint near miss) is given a `has_many` inverse, though its primary key allows at most one row per referenced row. codegen-relation-cardinality infers at-most-one only when the FK's columns are each unique or equal the full primary key; the general rule is that an FK whose column set contains any unique key of the referencing table (primary or unique) is at most one."
                    }

                    {
